# Batch is parsed line by line and is genuinely fragile about line endings near
# labels and block ends, so pin CRLF on the way out regardless of the platform
# that committed it. Everything else keeps LF in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Generated or binary: never touched.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary

# A captured terminal screen, kept BYTE FOR BYTE. Every line of it ends with a
# CR, and that CR is the whole subject of the test that reads it: treating a
# trailing CR as a spinner overwrite made every line of every pane read as
# blank. `text=auto eol=lf` above would quietly normalise the bug out of the
# fixture and leave a test that passes while proving nothing.
web/test/*.ansi -text
